      "faq": {
        "title": "FAQ",
        "q1": "How to upload files?",
        "a1": "Click any task card, then drag-drop or click to upload your Excel file. Supports .xlsx, .xls, .csv, .ods formats.",
        "q2": "Is my data safe?",
        "a2": "Absolutely! All file processing happens locally in your browser. Data is never uploaded to any server. The network monitor shows real-time if any data is transmitted externally.",
        "q3": "How to save processed files?",
        "a3": "After processing, click the 'Export' button and the file downloads directly to your device. No cloud intermediary.",
        "q4": "Are large files supported?",
        "a4": "Yes! It can handle files up to 100MB, with a free version limit of 5MB. For large files, it is recommended to use Chrome or Edge browsers.",
        "q5": "What output formats are supported?",
        "a5": "Export to Excel (with original styles), CSV, JSON, SQL INSERT, SQL IN query and more formats to meet different needs.",
        "q6": "What's the difference between Pipeline and Normal mode?",
        "a6": "Pipeline mode lets you combine multiple processing steps for complex workflows in one go. Normal mode is for single operations like one-time deduplication or masking. Pipeline is more efficient for complex needs."
      },
